    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d519">

                <pb facs="0647" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg562"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.0144/178</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bonillas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. E–4479</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: For the third time war aeroplanes of
                    the United States Army flew on the 5th instant over the City of Chihuahua <pb
                        facs="0648" n="563" xml:id="pg563"/> thereby arousing the natural
                    indignation of the inhabitants and authorities.</p>
                <p>Under special instructions from my Government, I have the honor to bring the
                    foregoing to Your Excellency’s knowledge and again drawing your attention to the
                    unpleasant frequency with which such occurrences are repeated, I beg you to urge
                    upon the authorities concerned the just necessity of stopping those unwarranted
                    abuses.</p>
                <p>Trusting that Your Excellency will see fit to take appropriate action, I thank
                    you in advance with pleasure therefor and renew [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Y. Bonillas</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
